 | Commit | Date | Change | Version |
 |---|---|---|---|
+| 4f4edcf35 | 2026-11-14 | STEP import meshes rational B-spline thread faces at full fidelity in seconds (about 10 K facets instead of 5-6 M per part, and no hole), splitting each parameter direction only where it is curved (PR #1638) | 0.20.0 |
+| 819ecfc31 | 2026-11-14 | A part moved into, added to, or un-tagged inside an operation's cut after generation no longer posts on a turned stock: the post judges the parts beside each op's source again and refuses by name (#1628, PR #1643) | 0.20.0 |
+| d08e9eda7 | 2026-11-14 | Carvera post: the first X/Y traverse after an `M6` tool change now comes after a `G0 Z` to the clearance height, not before it (#1616, PR #1661) | 0.20.0 |
+| c039a62c8 | 2026-11-14 | The Tormach mill post states the section's clearance Z before its first X/Y traverse after a tool change, and refuses (with no motion written) a stream that states no clearance or retract plane, so a tool too long for the work offset stops at the control's Z limit instead of rapiding through the part (PR #1618) | 0.20.0 |
+| bcf2d132a | 2026-11-14 | A closed STEP solid that the file winds inward now imports turned outward, and the import says so in its notes and on the status line (#1617) (PR #1671) | 0.20.0 |
+| 1f6a74be5 | 2026-11-14 | Trochoidal slot: a channel wider than twice the tool no longer leaves a post standing at its start; the bore now spirals out to the loop band (PR #1662) | 0.20.0 |
+| 389fe96c5 | 2026-11-14 | 2D Contour arcs at a coarse tolerance no longer pass a vertex on the part side, so a tessellated round wall verifies clean in both walk directions (#1579, PR #1658) | 0.20.0 |
+| b6c02115a | 2026-11-14 | STEP import refuses, by name, a closed shell whose mesh has a real gap and any face the kernel cannot mesh, and flips a face whose mesh is wound against its neighbours, instead of importing a model with walls missing or inside out (PR #1576) | 0.20.0 |
+| 350cfd205 | 2026-11-14 | Circular with entry Ramp now ramps along the ring at the ramp angle (3 deg by default) at every level, or dives at the plunge feed with a note; before, it fed straight down at the cutting feed (#1609, PR #1663) | 0.20.0 |
+| eee04e64b | 2026-11-14 | A 2D clearing no longer feeds across the part between two pieces of the cutter area whose walls are on one line (whole-model 2D Adaptive on Milling-test.step cut 0.94 mm into the part) (PR #1651) | 0.20.0 |
+| 5a387cffc | 2026-11-14 | A program that runs from one setup into the next now stops there by default (M0 with a comment naming the next setup); "Between setups" in the post options chooses an optional stop, running straight on, or one file per setup (#1532, PR #1650) | 0.20.0 |
+| d6ed0de73 | 2026-11-14 | A Face on the stock whose last row is tangent to the stock edge, with no part, no longer gets a false Gouge and posts (#1659) (PR #1668) | 0.20.0 |
+| 2b6e03f20 | 2026-11-14 | A 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive or 2D Offset with the stock as its source now clears the stock around the setup's parts, and does not cut through them (#1554, PR #1656) | 0.20.0 |
+| 57bdcf650 | 2026-11-14 | The whole-program post refuses by name when setups differ in End units, as it does for the Output and the thread output (#1540, PR #1653) | 0.20.0 |
+| 1bd9298d6 | 2026-11-14 | A part-source cross drill whose drill or approach enters another part in the setup is refused by name instead of posting (#1641, PR #1644) | 0.20.0 |
+| cfdf2ecec | 2026-11-14 | A cross drill taken off the stock is judged against the parts the stock holds, not against the stock: drilling a part's own cross hole off the raw bar now generates and posts, and a hole into a part where it models none is refused by name (#1635) (PR #1640) | 0.20.0 |
+| 8fe8181d5 | 2026-11-14 | A 2D Drill, Bore or Thread whose source is the stock is judged against the parts standing in that stock - it may enter a part only through the hole the part models there, to its size and depth - and a stock-source 2D Chamfer by the solid law, so a cut into a part is a blocking gouge on the operation and the post is refused even where the program sim cannot judge; a tap's core re-read no longer acquits a gouge in a neighbouring or stock-held part (#1631) (PR #1634) | 0.20.0 |
+| 53a77c9dc | 2026-11-14 | A 2D Engrave, Trace, Slot, Trochoidal slot, Circular, Contour or Face whose source is the stock (or a pick off it) is judged against the parts standing in that stock - a mark law for Engrave and Trace, the solid law for the rest - so a cut into a part is a blocking gouge on the operation and the post is refused even where the program sim cannot judge; a legal mark off the stock now posts on an aligned stock (#1607). A part-source 2D operation is also judged against the setup's other parts with the plain solid law, so a cut on one part that enters a neighbouring part is refused on the operation (#1621) (PR #1622) | 0.20.0 |
+| 7c07e8683 | 2026-11-14 | Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM, Sinumerik 840D and Heidenhain posts state the section's clearance Z (ClearancePlane, else RetractPlane) as a Z-only rapid, then X/Y at it, before the first X/Y traverse after each tool change; a stream that states neither plane is refused by name (#1633, #1616, PR #1636) | 0.20.0 |
+| 56a9b2f68 | 2026-11-14 | grblHAL, TinyG and Carvera posts state the section's clearance Z (ClearancePlane, else RetractPlane) before the first descent after a tool change (Carvera: after its X/Y traverse at the changer's exit height, which stays unverified), and refuse a stream that states neither by name (#1616, PR #1632) | 0.20.0 |
+| f318306b2 | 2026-11-14 | An Engrave or Trace on the finished part is judged as a mark (no deeper under the part's surface than the lesser of Top - Bottom and the cutter radius, and never to within 0.2 mm of the part's underside) and a 2D Pocket, Adaptive or Offset keeps the part under an area offset, extension or stock source: a deeper cut is a blocking gouge on the operation and the post is refused even where the program sim cannot judge; a legal engraving on a model now posts (#1595, #1603) (PR #1615) | 0.20.0 |
+| a3a59d1f6 | 2026-11-14 | 2D Contour and 2D Chamfer climb milling now runs climb with the M3 spindle - outside profiles clockwise, inside profiles counter-clockwise, G41 under control/wear compensation (BREAKING: posted direction reverses; projects that set climb off as a workaround now post conventional) (#1555, PR #1577) | 0.20.0 |
+| 22b8fe7a8 | 2026-11-14 | An operation whose hole list was edited to a value off the 1 um grid (e.g. an inch floor) no longer reads Stale after save and reopen (#1560, PR #1623) | 0.20.0 |
+| db6fd5d49 | 2026-11-14 | Failed project opens preserve the current document, history and filename (PR #1630) | 0.20.0 |
+| c00ba18a9 | 2026-11-14 | Circular posts each ring as two arcs (G2/G3) and its ramp entry as helical arcs on the ring, instead of 512 fixed chords per ring: a Ø6 hole drops from 74,131 moves to 417 (#1558, PR #1601) | 0.20.0 |
+| f2b42e3d3 | 2026-11-14 | The browser build opens models (STL, OBJ, STEP) and projects through an async file picker (#31) (PR #1314) | 0.20.0 |
+| 1943a22af | 2026-11-14 | 2D Adaptive has a Method choice - Spiral (default, unchanged) or Trochoidal, which clears a channel-like region with loops along its medial line, confined to the region and refused by name where one lane cannot cut it (PR #1598) | 0.20.0 |
+| 951cc5727 | 2026-11-14 | Work offsets are picked by number, up to what the setup's own post supports. The Setups page lists them as "Work offset n (NAME)", so Tormach shows 9. MCP `set_work_offset` takes a 1-based `index`; G54-G59 still work as aliases, and replies add `index` and `name`. (#931, PR #1124) | 0.20.0 |
+| 3e18717a8 | 2026-11-14 | Tormach mill posts lift Z straight up (`G53 G0 Z<safe>`) after every tool change, before the first X/Y or A move, so a low stored G30 never carries the tool sideways into the part (posted output changes: one line per tool change) (#1596, PR #1606) | 0.20.0 |
+| b08d73977 | 2026-11-14 | Work offsets are an index whose limit and names come from each setup's post. An offset the post cannot express is refused by setup name instead of posting at G54. Offsets 7 and up are saved as their number, and older builds cannot open those files. (#931, PR #1113) | 0.20.0 |
+| 745edc36a | 2026-11-14 | Tormach PathPilot mill programs now end with `G53 G0 Z0` then `M30`. The trailing `G30` is gone, so a low stored G30 position can no longer drive the tool back down at the end of the program (PR #1600) | 0.20.0 |
+| d5a8c518e | 2026-11-14 | A Trochoidal slot on the finished part (whole model or pick) is now judged against it: a channel typed through a wall or below the floor is a blocking gouge on the operation and the post is refused, even where the program sim cannot judge (#1593) (PR #1597) | 0.20.0 |
+| f84059c97 | 2026-11-14 | Browser build: Save and Save As download the project, Post downloads the NC program, and file commands the browser cannot run yet are greyed with the reason instead of doing nothing (#1431, PR #1438) | 0.20.0 |
+| a6562c359 | 2026-11-14 | Posts receive the work offset as a 1-based number and write their own word; the Tormach mill and lathe posts accept work offsets 7-9 (G59.1-G59.3), and a post that cannot express an offset refuses it by setup name (#931, slice 1, PR #1101) | 0.20.0 |
+| 37bf5b429 | 2026-11-14 | STEP import no longer refuses healthy models whose faces need many evaluations (the per-face cap is now 150 M); a finer pass that runs out on a provably continuous face keeps the coarser mesh, and a face that may jump is still refused by name (#1568, PR #1578) | 0.20.0 |
+| be27a4c7e | 2026-11-14 | A Bore op refuses, by name, a hole wider than 3 x its tool diameter (+ 2 x stock to leave; less for a bull nose or ball on a through hole, judged at its reach on the floor). Its one ring would leave a free core, which it used to post as ok. Detect holes leaves such holes out of a Bore op and names each one (MCP `skipped`) (PR #1575) | 0.20.0 |
+| 7bfb18246 | 2026-11-13 | A Circular whose picked floor (or whole-model source) it would cut below is now judged against the model: the gouge is reported on the operation and the post is refused (#1550, #1543) (PR #1585) | 0.20.0 |
